            "review_title": "Review at Cafe 343",
            "review_text": "LamN\nSingapore, Singapore4905 contributions\n0\nGreat place to watch the local HCMC middle class\nMar 2018 • Friends\nWell-to-do but not super-rich (ie. 2-wheeler not Bentley owners with chauffeurs) locals, especially those in their 40’s and above, would not go to Starbucks, RuNam, Trung Nguyên, etc, to meet their friends and relatives. They would come to a place like 343, where they can hang out in comfort, and spend short moments or long hours chatting, smoking (in designated sections). \n\nLarge selection of beverages - freshly-pressed juices, smoothies and delicious coffee drinks. The food is traditional ‘all day’ Việt dishes - various noodle soups, broken rice dishes (cơm tấm), bánh mì, fresh fruits, etc. If you wish for an item that is not on the menu, you can always ask the very loyal staff. (Language barriers aside) they will happily accommodate, especially vegetarian dishes as the owner is vegetarian.\n\nIt’s almost like a home away from home for many locals, and hence is open from 7 am to 11 pm 7 days a week. Prices are very reasonable for the quality.\nRead more\nWritten March 31, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
